4. Trailing commas after the last field in a signature declaration are not allowed in Alloy 6 and will trigger syntax errors; always ensure the closing brace follows the last field directly.
5. Persistent syntax errors in predicate headers usually result from missing or incorrect type annotations for parameters in Alloy 6. Always check that every parameter in a predicate header is explicitly typed and the delimiter (comma) is used correctly.

